#### 24.1.3 Stirling Numbers of the First Kind

I. Definitions

A. \((-1)^{n-n}\)S\({}_{n}^{(m)}\) is the number of permutations of \(n\) symbols which have exactly \(m\) cycles.

B. Generating functions

\[x(x{-}1)\ldots(x{-}n{+}1){=}\mathop{\sum}\limits_{n=0}^{n}S_{n}^{(m)}x^{m}\]

\[\{\ln\,(1{+}x)\}^{n}{=}m!\mathop{\sum}\limits_{n=m}^{\infty}S_{n}^{(m)}\mathop{ \pi}\limits_{n}^{n}\mathop{\pi}\limits_{n}^{n}\mathop{\pi}\limits_{n}^{n} \mathop{\pi}\limits_{n}^{n}\mathop{\pi}\limits_{n}^{n}\mathop{\pi}\limits_{n}^{ \left|x\right|}{<}1\]

C. Closed form (see closed form for \(\mathop{\mbox{\boldmath$S$}}\limits_{n}^{(m)}\))

\[S_{n}^{(m)}{=}\mathop{\sum}\limits_{k=0}^{n-m}(-1)^{k}\mathop{\left(n-1{+}k \right)}\mathop{\left(n-m-k\right)}\mathop{\mbox{\boldmath$S$}}\limits_{n-m-k }^{\left(n\right)}\mathop{\mbox{\boldmath$S$}}\limits_{n-m+k}^{\left(n\right)}\]

